# night_siege — 3.17's worked function+hook example (docs/COMMANDS.md §5.1/§5.2).
# Bound to DayNight's night_started signal by content/hooks/night_siege.tres, which ships
# disabled (enabled = false) — flip that .tres to try it, or run `function night_siege` by hand
# any time regardless of the hook's own enabled flag.
#
# "Announce" reuses the surface commands already have for it: a CommandResult's own message is
# what reaches whoever's watching (the console, run_commands.gd's --json output, a future admin
# UI) — COMMANDS.md §8 keeps chat out of scope on purpose, so there is no separate broadcast verb
# to call here. `wave start`'s own success line ("wave started: N enemies") IS the announcement.
wave start 10
